{"nodes": [{"id": "actions_revocarAcceso", "label": "revocarAcceso Server Action", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/modules/refunds/actions.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Admin-only refund flow: sets order+enrollment to refunded, reverses instructor earnings, revokes the certificate (and deletes its R2 PDF), then emails the buyer only if the order was not already refunded."}, {"id": "actions_refundIdempotencyPattern", "label": "In-Transaction Idempotency Check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/modules/refunds/actions.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WHY: the eligibility SELECT that decides idempotency is repeated INSIDE the transaction (same pattern as aprobarPago in billing/actions.ts) so two overlapping calls to revocarAcceso can't double-send the refund email - the second tx blocks on the orders UPDATE and then sees status='refunded' and returns early. A cheap precheck outside the tx only short-circuits 'not found / not paid' without paying the tx cost."}, {"id": "certification_issuance_revocarCertificadoTx", "label": "revocarCertificadoTx (certification/issuance)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/modules/refunds/actions.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "lib_r2_deleteObject", "label": "deleteObject (lib/r2)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/modules/refunds/actions.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deletes the revoked certificate's PDF from Cloudflare R2; failure is logged but does not fail the refund."}, {"id": "module_refunds_actions", "label": "refunds/actions.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/modules/refunds/actions.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null,